Not quite.

84
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:01,680
No.

85
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:10,800
So the way we view about money and spend and channels is we actually view, yes, we have the top down view, but we're mainly thinking bottoms up.

86
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:14,960
And so we treat each channel as its own growth engine.

87
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:18,160
And actually our biggest one still is Google and Google search.

88
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:24,080
And so what we're doing is like that, we're obsessed with, okay, how do we make really great ag copy?

89
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,160
How do we localize it to all the geos?

90
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:28,720
How do we have really high converging landing pages?

91
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:31,840
And then it's like, okay, week over week, how do you scale it?

92
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:38,960
Ten percent, twenty percent for Netta, it's a similar one where, yes, you want a great amount of creative, but you also want to have a great amount of creative.

93
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,160
But you're also on really high quality.

94
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:46,720
And then when I think about scaling creative in order to see that unlock, what you actually want to do is more segmentation.

95
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:49,760
So you're maybe using AI to help.

96
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:58,240
Before maybe if you just had a general like, here's how to make images and videos with AI, but now you can go that one level deeper.

97
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:04,240
Like, here's how podcasters or here's how people making apps can create with image and video.

98
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:08,320
And you can use AI to do that like personalization segmentation.

99
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:11,920
The other really big unlock for us has been the localization side.

100
00:10:12,560 --> 00:10:14,400
And that's where we've really lent into AI.

101
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:25,120
As a side note, we initially went down the route of like, you pay an expensive SAS app for localization, you pay for an agency, so then who have people to localize it.

102
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:31,920
But I kept on having our team just sending screenshots of ChatGPT saying, Oh, we should use this phrasing instead is way better.

103
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:37,200
And I was like, Well, if the LLMs are way better at translation than these agencies and expensive tooling.

104
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:40,640
So we actually ripped out all the localization infrastructure.

105
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:46,880
We built our own GitHub action and there's like a thin library which just extract the strings.

106
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,480
or wraps all the strings.

107
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:56,480
And then each time we make a PR to our repo, it just sends it with like a prompt per language about the localization guide.

108
00:10:56,880 --> 00:11:00,720
And that means we're able to localize like way cheaper and much faster.

109
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:11,280
And then once we've also localized the apps, you'll then be able to localize all the ads, there's stuff like our dubbing model or again just like passing the copy with good prompts gets fantastic results.

110
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:12,720
You know, we think bottoms up.

111
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:18,560
What's that next bottleneck for us to like scale another twenty percent week on week, month on month?

